    "seq": 163,
    "contract_id": "batch-critic.v2",
    "field": "/cases/*/case",
    "marker": "n/a",
    "value": "SRC_002's argument that both idempotency and safety are necessary rests on the claim that 'idempotency without safety permits transient inconsistency observable to concurrent replays.' But transient inconsistency during concurrent access is an isolation/atomicity concern, not a safety concern. An op"
   },
   {
